From: WelsonJS
Subject: [PATCH] Windows build: resources for the binaries and MSVC fixes

Windows-specific changes: an icon for the executables and version information
for every executable and DLL, MSVC options and warnings, and building with
clang against the Visual Studio 2019 STL.

1. cmake : Windows icon and version information for every executable and DLL

  llama.cpp has no Windows resource files, so its executables and DLLs have no
  icon and no version information (the "Description" in the file properties is
  empty).

  Add cmake/win-resources.cmake, included at the end of the top-level
  CMakeLists.txt, after all targets are defined. It collects every executable,
  shared library and module library of the build (ggml, ggml-base, the CPU
  backends, llama, llama-common, mtmd, the tools and their -impl libraries) and
  gives each its own resource script. Cache options:

    - LLAMA_WIN_ICON: an .ico file, embedded as the application icon of the
      executables. It is copied next to the resource scripts, which start with
      #pragma code_page(65001), so a build folder with non-ASCII characters
      works regardless of the ANSI code page.
    - LLAMA_WIN_DESCRIPTION: a text for the version information, which is added
      when it is set. FileDescription is "<target> - <role> (<text>)", where
      <role> says what the binary is (for example "ggml CPU backend, haswell
      variant"; omitted for a target it does not know), ProductName is
      "llama.cpp", InternalName and OriginalFilename come from the target, and
      Comments gives the text, LLAMA_BUILD_COMMIT and LLAMA_BUILD_NUMBER.
    - LLAMA_WIN_VERSION: FileVersion and ProductVersion (a.b.c.d); without it,
      0.0.<LLAMA_BUILD_NUMBER>.0.
    - LLAMA_WIN_COMPANY, LLAMA_WIN_COPYRIGHT: CompanyName and LegalCopyright,
      when set.

  The resource uses numeric FILEOS/FILETYPE values (VFT_APP for executables,
  VFT_DLL for DLLs) instead of the winver.h names, so no include path is needed
  (rc.exe and llvm-rc). The scripts are written through configure_file, which
  only touches a file when its content changes, so a new CMake run does not
  relink. With LLAMA_WIN_ICON and LLAMA_WIN_DESCRIPTION empty (the default) the
  build is unchanged.

2. ggml-cpu : do not pass unsupported options to MSVC

  Two compiler options in ggml/src/ggml-cpu/CMakeLists.txt produce warning
  D9002 ("ignoring unknown option") with MSVC:

    - /arch:SSE4.2 for the sse42 CPU variant exists only in newer MSVC. MSVC
      19.29 (Visual Studio 2019, the AppVeyor image) ignores it for every
      source file of that variant. Add it only when check_c_compiler_flag
      accepts it; CMake treats D9002 as a failed check. Without the option the
      variant is compiled for SSE2 code generation, which is safe: MSVC accepts
      SSE4 intrinsics with any /arch, and the variant is chosen at run time only
      on CPUs with SSE4.2.
    - -fno-lto for the CPU feature detection objects is a GCC/clang option.
      Pass it only when not MSVC; MSVC does not use LTO unless /GL is given.

3. llama : fix a size_t truncation, and disable MSVC conversion warnings like ggml

  MSVC reports many C4244 ("possible loss of data") warnings in the llama,
  mtmd and other targets (for example std::fill of a float vector with 0.0 or
  0 in tools/mtmd/mtmd-audio.cpp, or std::pair<int64_t, uint32_t> from an
  int64_t in src/llama-model.cpp). Almost all are harmless and are the same in
  upstream llama.cpp. ggml/CMakeLists.txt already disables C4244, C4267 and
  C4305 (among others) for the ggml targets; do the same in the top-level
  CMakeLists.txt, before src, common and tools are added. MSVC only, so clang
  (the ARM64 build) is not affected.

  One of these warnings is a real truncation, fixed here:

    - src/llama-quant.cpp, llama_tensor_dequantize_impl: the worker lambda took
      the element count as int, but it is passed a size_t (thr_elems), and the
      functions it calls (to_float, ggml_fp16_to_fp32_row,
      ggml_bf16_to_fp32_row) take int64_t. A thread with more than 2^31 - 1
      elements (requantizing a very large tensor with few threads) would get a
      wrong count. Take int64_t.

4. common : build jinja value_func_t with the Visual Studio 2019 STL

  value_func_t (common/jinja/value.h) calls std::function::target<func_hptr>(),
  where func_hptr is a function type. With clang and the MSVC 14.29 STL
  (Visual Studio 2019, the AppVeyor image; the ARM64 build) this fails:

    functional:1140: error: reinterpret_cast from 'const void *' to
    'std::shared_ptr<jinja::value_t> (*)(const jinja::func_args &)' casts away
    qualifiers

  Newer STLs (14.44, 14.51) compile it. It also never matches: std::function
  stores a plain function as a function pointer, so the target type is
  func_hptr *. Add function_pointer(), which asks for target<func_hptr *>() and
  returns the stored function pointer (nullptr for another callable), and use
  it in unique_hash() and equivalent(), which the comments describe as
  comparing function pointers. Both are unused for now.

Apply with: git -c core.autocrlf=false apply <this file>

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index 81f23d7..11d28f9 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -193,6 +193,16 @@ endif()
 # build the library
 #
 
+# MSVC: disable the conversion warnings that ggml/CMakeLists.txt also disables
+# for the ggml targets (MSVC_WARNING_FLAGS), for llama, common and the tools.
+if (MSVC)
+    add_compile_options(
+        /wd4244  # Conversion from one type to another type, possible loss of data
+        /wd4267  # Conversion from 'size_t' to a smaller type, possible loss of data
+        /wd4305  # Conversion from 'type1' to 'type2', possible loss of data
+    )
+endif()
+
 add_subdirectory(src)
 
 #
@@ -280,3 +290,7 @@ configure_file(cmake/llama.pc.in
 
 install(FILES "${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}/llama.pc"
         DESTINATION ${CMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR}/pkgconfig)
+
+# Windows icon and version information for the executables and DLLs; after all
+# targets are defined.
+include(cmake/win-resources.cmake)
diff --git a/cmake/win-resources.cmake b/cmake/win-resources.cmake
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..99e88f3
--- /dev/null
+++ b/cmake/win-resources.cmake
@@ -0,0 +1,175 @@
+# Windows resources for every executable and DLL of the build: an icon for the
+# executables and version information for all of them. Included at the end of
+# the top-level CMakeLists.txt, after all targets are defined.
+#
+#   LLAMA_WIN_ICON         .ico file embedded as the application icon of the executables
+#   LLAMA_WIN_DESCRIPTION  text for the version information, for example "llama.cpp built
+#                          for WelsonJS": the description becomes "<target> - <role> (<text>)"
+#   LLAMA_WIN_VERSION      file and product version (a.b.c.d); default 0.0.<build number>.0
+#   LLAMA_WIN_COMPANY      CompanyName
+#   LLAMA_WIN_COPYRIGHT    LegalCopyright
+#
+# The version information is added when LLAMA_WIN_DESCRIPTION is set.
+
+set(LLAMA_WIN_ICON        "" CACHE FILEPATH "llama: .ico file embedded in the Windows executables")
+set(LLAMA_WIN_DESCRIPTION "" CACHE STRING   "llama: text for the version information of the Windows executables and DLLs")
+set(LLAMA_WIN_VERSION     "" CACHE STRING   "llama: version (a.b.c.d) in the version information (default: 0.0.<build number>.0)")
+set(LLAMA_WIN_COMPANY     "" CACHE STRING   "llama: CompanyName in the version information")
+set(LLAMA_WIN_COPYRIGHT   "" CACHE STRING   "llama: LegalCopyright in the version information")
+
+# Executables and DLLs (shared and module libraries) defined in dir and below.
+function(llama_win_collect_binaries dir out)
+    get_property(targets DIRECTORY "${dir}" PROPERTY BUILDSYSTEM_TARGETS)
+    set(result "")
+    foreach (target IN LISTS targets)
+        get_target_property(type ${target} TYPE)
+        if (type STREQUAL "EXECUTABLE" OR type STREQUAL "SHARED_LIBRARY" OR type STREQUAL "MODULE_LIBRARY")
+            list(APPEND result ${target})
+        endif()
+    endforeach()
+    get_property(subdirs DIRECTORY "${dir}" PROPERTY SUBDIRECTORIES)
+    foreach (subdir IN LISTS subdirs)
+        llama_win_collect_binaries("${subdir}" sub)
+        list(APPEND result ${sub})
+    endforeach()
+    set(${out} ${result} PARENT_SCOPE)
+endfunction()
+
+# What a binary is, for its file description ("" when not known).
+function(llama_win_role target out)
+    set(role "")
+    if (target STREQUAL "ggml")
+        set(role "ggml tensor library")
+    elseif (target STREQUAL "ggml-base")
+        set(role "ggml base library")
+    elseif (target STREQUAL "ggml-cpu")
+        set(role "ggml CPU backend")
+    elseif (target MATCHES "^ggml-cpu-(.+)$")
+        set(role "ggml CPU backend, ${CMAKE_MATCH_1} variant")
+    elseif (target MATCHES "^ggml-(.+)$")
+        set(role "ggml ${CMAKE_MATCH_1} backend")
+    elseif (target STREQUAL "llama")
+        set(role "llama.cpp library")
+    elseif (target STREQUAL "llama-common")
+        set(role "llama.cpp common library")
+    elseif (target STREQUAL "mtmd")
+        set(role "llama.cpp multimodal library")
+    elseif (target MATCHES "^(.+)-impl$")
+        set(role "${CMAKE_MATCH_1} implementation library")
+    elseif (target STREQUAL "llama-server")
+        set(role "OpenAI-compatible LLM server")
+    elseif (target STREQUAL "llama-cli")
+        set(role "LLM command-line interface")
+    elseif (target STREQUAL "llama-quantize")
+        set(role "GGUF model quantizer")
+    endif()
+    set(${out} "${role}" PARENT_SCOPE)
+endfunction()
+
+if (WIN32 AND (LLAMA_WIN_ICON OR LLAMA_WIN_DESCRIPTION))
+    set(llama_win_res_dir "${CMAKE_BINARY_DIR}/win-resources")
+    file(MAKE_DIRECTORY "${llama_win_res_dir}")
+
+    if (LLAMA_WIN_ICON)
+        if (NOT EXISTS "${LLAMA_WIN_ICON}")
+            message(FATAL_ERROR "LLAMA_WIN_ICON does not exist: ${LLAMA_WIN_ICON}")
+        endif()
+        # Copy the icon next to the resource scripts, which are UTF-8, so a path
+        # with non-ASCII characters does not depend on the ANSI code page.
+        configure_file("${LLAMA_WIN_ICON}" "${llama_win_res_dir}/llama-icon.ico" COPYONLY)
+    endif()
+
+    set(llama_win_build "${LLAMA_BUILD_NUMBER}")
+    if (NOT llama_win_build MATCHES "^[0-9]+$")
+        set(llama_win_build 0)
+    endif()
+    if (LLAMA_WIN_VERSION)
+        if (NOT LLAMA_WIN_VERSION MATCHES "^[0-9]+\\.[0-9]+\\.[0-9]+\\.[0-9]+$")
+            message(FATAL_ERROR "LLAMA_WIN_VERSION must be a.b.c.d: ${LLAMA_WIN_VERSION}")
+        endif()
+        set(llama_win_version "${LLAMA_WIN_VERSION}")
+    else()
+        # As in LLAMA_INSTALL_VERSION (0.0.<build number>).
+        set(llama_win_version "0.0.${llama_win_build}.0")
+    endif()
+    string(REPLACE "." "," llama_win_version_numbers "${llama_win_version}")
+
+    # A double quote inside a resource string is written as two.
+    string(REPLACE "\"" "\"\"" llama_win_desc      "${LLAMA_WIN_DESCRIPTION}")
+    string(REPLACE "\"" "\"\"" llama_win_commit    "${LLAMA_BUILD_COMMIT}")
+    string(REPLACE "\"" "\"\"" llama_win_company   "${LLAMA_WIN_COMPANY}")
+    string(REPLACE "\"" "\"\"" llama_win_copyright "${LLAMA_WIN_COPYRIGHT}")
+
+    llama_win_collect_binaries("${CMAKE_SOURCE_DIR}" llama_win_binaries)
+    foreach (target IN LISTS llama_win_binaries)
+        get_target_property(type ${target} TYPE)
+        get_target_property(output_name ${target} OUTPUT_NAME)
+        if (NOT output_name)
+            set(output_name ${target})
+        endif()
+        if (type STREQUAL "EXECUTABLE")
+            set(file_name "${output_name}.exe")
+            set(file_type "0x1")    # VFT_APP
+        else()
+            set(file_name "${output_name}.dll")
+            set(file_type "0x2")    # VFT_DLL
+        endif()
+
+        set(rc "#pragma code_page(65001)\n")
+        if (LLAMA_WIN_ICON AND type STREQUAL "EXECUTABLE")
+            string(APPEND rc "1 ICON \"${llama_win_res_dir}/llama-icon.ico\"\n")
+        endif()
+        if (LLAMA_WIN_DESCRIPTION)
+            llama_win_role(${target} role)
+            if (role)
+                set(description "${target} - ${role} (${llama_win_desc})")
+            else()
+                set(description "${target} (${llama_win_desc})")
+            endif()
+            # Numeric values instead of winver.h names (0x40004 = VOS_NT_WINDOWS32),
+            # so no include path is needed (rc.exe and llvm-rc).
+            string(APPEND rc
+                "1 VERSIONINFO\n"
+                "FILEVERSION ${llama_win_version_numbers}\n"
+                "PRODUCTVERSION ${llama_win_version_numbers}\n"
+                "FILEFLAGSMASK 0x3F\n"
+                "FILEFLAGS 0x0\n"
+                "FILEOS 0x40004\n"
+                "FILETYPE ${file_type}\n"
+                "FILESUBTYPE 0x0\n"
+                "BEGIN\n"
+                "    BLOCK \"StringFileInfo\"\n"
+                "    BEGIN\n"
+                "        BLOCK \"040904B0\"\n"
+                "        BEGIN\n")
+            if (LLAMA_WIN_COMPANY)
+                string(APPEND rc "            VALUE \"CompanyName\", \"${llama_win_company}\"\n")
+            endif()
+            string(APPEND rc
+                "            VALUE \"FileDescription\", \"${description}\"\n"
+                "            VALUE \"FileVersion\", \"${llama_win_version}\"\n"
+                "            VALUE \"InternalName\", \"${target}\"\n")
+            if (LLAMA_WIN_COPYRIGHT)
+                string(APPEND rc "            VALUE \"LegalCopyright\", \"${llama_win_copyright}\"\n")
+            endif()
+            string(APPEND rc
+                "            VALUE \"OriginalFilename\", \"${file_name}\"\n"
+                "            VALUE \"ProductName\", \"llama.cpp\"\n"
+                "            VALUE \"ProductVersion\", \"${llama_win_version}\"\n"
+                "            VALUE \"Comments\", \"${llama_win_desc}. llama.cpp ${llama_win_commit}, build ${llama_win_build}.\"\n"
+                "        END\n"
+                "    END\n"
+                "    BLOCK \"VarFileInfo\"\n"
+                "    BEGIN\n"
+                "        VALUE \"Translation\", 0x409, 1200\n"
+                "    END\n"
+                "END\n")
+        endif()
+        # Write through configure_file, which only touches the file when it
+        # changes, so a new CMake run does not relink every binary.
+        file(WRITE "${llama_win_res_dir}/${target}.rc.in" "${rc}")
+        configure_file("${llama_win_res_dir}/${target}.rc.in" "${llama_win_res_dir}/${target}.rc" COPYONLY)
+        target_sources(${target} PRIVATE "${llama_win_res_dir}/${target}.rc")
+    endforeach()
+    message(STATUS "Windows resources (version ${llama_win_version}; icon: ${LLAMA_WIN_ICON}; description: ${LLAMA_WIN_DESCRIPTION}): ${llama_win_binaries}")
+endif()
diff --git a/common/jinja/value.h b/common/jinja/value.h
index 5cf85e4..5a36857 100644
--- a/common/jinja/value.h
+++ b/common/jinja/value.h
@@ -717,7 +717,7 @@ struct value_func_t : public value_t {
     virtual hasher unique_hash() const noexcept override {
         // Note: this is unused for now, we don't support function as object keys
         // use function pointer as unique identifier
-        const auto target = val_func.target<func_hptr>();
+        const auto target = function_pointer(val_func);
         return hasher(typeid(*this)).update(&target, sizeof(target));
     }
 protected:
@@ -725,10 +725,20 @@ protected:
         // Note: this is unused for now, we don't support function as object keys
         // compare function pointers
         // (val_func == other.val_func does not work as std::function::operator== is only used for nullptr check)
-        const auto target_this  = this->val_func.target<func_hptr>();
-        const auto target_other = other.val_func.target<func_hptr>();
+        const auto target_this  = function_pointer(this->val_func);
+        const auto target_other = function_pointer(other.val_func);
         return typeid(*this) == typeid(other) && target_this == target_other;
     }
+private:
+    // The plain function a func_handler holds, or nullptr for another callable.
+    // std::function stores a plain function as a function pointer, so the target
+    // type is func_hptr * (target<func_hptr>() never matches). It also compiles
+    // with the Visual Studio 2019 STL, whose target<function type>() fails with
+    // clang ("reinterpret_cast ... casts away qualifiers").
+    static func_hptr * function_pointer(const func_handler & func) {
+        const auto target = func.target<func_hptr *>();
+        return target ? *target : nullptr;
+    }
 };
 using value_func = std::shared_ptr<value_func_t>;
 
diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/CMakeLists.txt b/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/CMakeLists.txt
index 55f0f5a..6e0fec5 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -13,7 +13,11 @@ function(ggml_add_cpu_backend_features cpu_name arch)
     # from inlining architecture-specific instructions into the score function.
     # Without this, LTO can cause SIGILL when loading backends on older CPUs
     # (e.g., loading power10 backend on power9 crashes before feature check runs).
-    target_compile_options(${GGML_CPU_FEATS_NAME} PRIVATE -fno-lto)
+    # -fno-lto is a GCC/clang option; MSVC warns about it (D9002) and does not
+    # use LTO unless /GL is given.
+    if (NOT MSVC)
+        target_compile_options(${GGML_CPU_FEATS_NAME} PRIVATE -fno-lto)
+    endif()
     target_link_libraries(${cpu_name} PRIVATE ${GGML_CPU_FEATS_NAME})
 endfunction()
 
@@ -300,7 +304,14 @@ function(ggml_add_cpu_backend_variant_impl tag_name)
                 list(APPEND ARCH_FLAGS /arch:AVX)
                 list(APPEND ARCH_DEFINITIONS GGML_AVX)
             elseif (GGML_SSE42)
-                list(APPEND ARCH_FLAGS /arch:SSE4.2)
+                # /arch:SSE4.2 exists only in newer MSVC; MSVC 19.29 (Visual
+                # Studio 2019) ignores it with warning D9002. The variant still
+                # builds without it: MSVC accepts SSE4 intrinsics with any /arch.
+                include(CheckCCompilerFlag)
+                check_c_compiler_flag("/arch:SSE4.2" GGML_MSVC_HAS_ARCH_SSE42)
+                if (GGML_MSVC_HAS_ARCH_SSE42)
+                    list(APPEND ARCH_FLAGS /arch:SSE4.2)
+                endif()
                 list(APPEND ARCH_DEFINITIONS GGML_SSE42)
             endif()
             if (GGML_AVX_VNNI)
diff --git a/src/llama-quant.cpp b/src/llama-quant.cpp
index 897c904..3622f9c 100644
--- a/src/llama-quant.cpp
+++ b/src/llama-quant.cpp
@@ -264,7 +264,7 @@ static void llama_tensor_dequantize_impl(
         size_t thr_elems = thr_blocks * block_size; // number of elements for this thread
         size_t thr_block_bytes = thr_blocks * block_size_bytes; // number of input bytes for this thread
 
-        auto compute = [qtype] (ggml_type typ, uint8_t * inbuf, float * outbuf, int nels) {
+        auto compute = [qtype] (ggml_type typ, uint8_t * inbuf, float * outbuf, int64_t nels) {
             if (typ == GGML_TYPE_F16) {
                 ggml_fp16_to_fp32_row((ggml_fp16_t *)inbuf, outbuf, nels);
             } else if (typ == GGML_TYPE_BF16) {
